# Agent Instructions

## Purpose

> **Scope:** Agent-facing entry point for authoring and maintaining this repository.
> **Key items:** repository layout, skill registration, local workspace, improvement,
> boundaries.

This repository is {{collection-title}}, a collection of Agent Skills packages.

Each member skill lives under `skills/<name>/` and carries its own `SKILL.md` router
read by agents that use the skill.

The root `SKILL.md` is the collection index - it lists member skills and routes to
them.

This file is the entry point for agents that modify the collection.

## Repository Layout

| Path                         | Role                                          |
|------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| `SKILL.md`                   | Collection index and router to member skills  |
| `AGENTS.md`                  | This file - agent entry point for maintenance |
| `README.md`                  | Human-facing overview and directory tree      |
| `process/member-contract.md` | Shared member-skill behavior contract         |
| `process/session-review.md`  | Collection-level session-review procedure     |
| `process/synchronization.md` | Member and collection fetch/merge/push        |
| `skills/<name>/`             | One directory per member skill package        |
| `work/`                      | Gitignored local workspace (see below)        |

## Adding a Skill

- Create `skills/<name>/` with its own `SKILL.md` carrying valid frontmatter (`name`,
  `description`, `metadata.version`).
- Register the skill in the root `SKILL.md` skills table and mirror it in the
  `README.md` tree in the same change set.
- Keep each skill self-contained: a member skill never reaches into a sibling skill's
  directory or into `work/`.
- Member skills are always external repositories: each skill's contents live and change
  only in its own repository, the collection records the pinned submodule commit, and a
  skill's files are never authored or edited inside the collection.

## Local Workspace

Temporary files, research scratch, and throwaway scripts live in the gitignored `work/`
directory, organized by date: `work/YYYY-MM/YYYY-MM-DD/` for the day the artifact was
created.

Shipped files never reference `work/` content.

## Improving the Collection

- "improve {{collection-name}}" or "improve the collection" runs
  `process/session-review.md` - gather, partition by owner, delegate member lessons,
  gate index lessons, apply, validate, report.
- A member lesson is applied only through that member's own session-review procedure,
  running against the member's repository checkout.
- An index lesson changes only root files, within the registration and version rules
  in Boundaries below.

## Boundaries

- A bare `work on {{collection-name}}` request that names no operation is standby -
  read this file and `SKILL.md`, confirm readiness, and wait for the named operation.
- Never embed real names, paths, or project identifiers supplied with a request -
  create anonymized examples instead.
- Member skills keep the shared review-mode convention and the behavior contract in
  `process/member-contract.md`. A member that gains or changes this surface keeps the
  shared semantics and records any deliberate variance in its own documents.
- The collection version is stored once, in `metadata.version` of the root `SKILL.md`.
  Member versions are read from each member's own `SKILL.md` at load time, never
  copied into collection documents.
- Any change to a project document bumps that project's version, but at most once
  between two commits.
- In prose, prefer a comma or a period between clauses - a spaced hyphen (` - `) marks
  an aside or a definitional separator, never a clause join.
- Do not claim validation that did not run.
- Never commit automatically - propose a one-sentence commit message and let the user
  commit.
